  "reviews": [
    {
      "reviewtitle": "Thanks for uploading this. \ud83d\udd25\ud83d\udc4d",
      "reviewbody": "neat. sorry, not much to say. Just thought it was cool that somebody uploaded a 16mm film scan of steamboat willie. and the comment section seemed empty, so figured I might just give it something so it didn't look so empty. \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "BookWyrm33",
      "reviewdate": "2024-01-14 15:50:35",
      "createdate": "2024-01-14 15:50:35",
      "reviewer_itemname": "@bookwyrm33"
    },
    {
      "reviewtitle": "I love this",
      "reviewbody": "It's great to see this archived and preserved in such high quality. It really gives you the ability to see just how much work and technology went into these.",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "breakingitdown",
      "reviewdate": "2024-01-15 16:17:37",
      "createdate": "2024-01-15 16:17:37",
      "reviewer_itemname": "@breakitdownforme"
    },
    {
      "reviewtitle": "frame by frame: and with visible soundtrack",
      "reviewbody": "\nThis is nifty, and can step each frame.   great.    Love the visible soundtrack.\n\ntoot'ed: https://mastodon.archive.org/@brewsterkahle/111768093985792235",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "brewster",
      "reviewdate": "2024-01-16 23:38:01",
      "createdate": "2024-01-16 23:38:01",
      "reviewer_itemname": "@brewster"
    },
    {
      "reviewtitle": "A Special Moment",
      "reviewbody": "\"Steamboat Willie\" is indeed one of the finest cartoons of its time.",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "Thundera87",
      "reviewdate": "2024-01-17 20:26:37",
      "createdate": "2024-01-17 20:26:37",
      "reviewer_itemname": "@thundera87"
    },
    {
      "reviewtitle": "Incomplete ersion",
      "reviewbody": "Excludes opening and closing cards and pig-accordion nipple-playing scene (@5:39:22). Interesting though to see how the censored print plays. Otherwise, an authentic 24 fps scan with scratches and dust particles preserved. Hay truck reveals a small-cap \"D\" before the word \"HAY\" that is mostly cropped out of other prints (@2:39:05).",
      "stars": "4",
      "reviewer": "G. James Berigan",
      "reviewdate": "2024-01-22 21:39:15",
      "createdate": "2024-01-22 21:39:15",
      "reviewer_itemname": "@g_james_berigan"
    }
  ],
